<article class="env-remark" id="05GJ">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05GJ">Remark <span data-tag="05GJ">10.1.3.15</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be an $\infty $-category and let $n$ be an integer. Using Proposition <a data-tag="05GH" href="/tag/05GH">10.1.3.14</a>, we see that the condition that a simplicial object $X_{\bullet }$ of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is $n$-skeletal depends only on the restriction of $X_{\bullet }$ to the (non-full) subcategory $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{\mathrm{surj}})^{\operatorname{op}} \subset \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }})^{\operatorname{op}}$ (see Notation <a data-tag="04ZR" href="/tag/04ZR">1.1.2.12</a>). Stated more informally (and slightly incorrectly), the condition of $n$-skeletality depends only on the degeneracy operators of $X_{\bullet }$, and not on its face operators. </p>
